WEBVTT

1
00:00:26.081 --> 00:00:28.792
(SCREAMING)

2
00:00:31.128 --> 00:00:35.424
(JUNGLE-STYLE MUSIC)

3
00:00:47.686 --> 00:00:49.772
(SCREAM)

4
00:02:21.321 --> 00:02:25.284
(RADIO ON - BLARING POP SONG)

5
00:02:43.969 --> 00:02:46.430
(TAP SQUEAKS)

6
00:03:00.861 --> 00:03:05.449
(RADIO MUSIC CONTINUES)

7
00:03:26.303 --> 00:03:28.597
(ALARM BUZZES)

8
00:03:29.264 --> 00:03:32.184
(WHEELS WHIRRING)

9
00:03:47.157 --> 00:03:50.452
(WHIRR OF BIKE WHEELS)

10
00:04:17.271 --> 00:04:20.274
(MECHANISM WHINES)

11
00:04:38.751 --> 00:04:41.086
Ha-ha-ha! Ha-ha!

12
00:04:42.046 --> 00:04:47.926
You missed! You missed this time.
you little menace!

13
00:04:48.093 --> 00:04:50.012
I beat you!

14
00:04:53.015 --> 00:04:54.558
Morning.

15
00:05:07.863 --> 00:05:12.910
- You're getting upset over nothing!
- I'm not.

16
00:05:13.077 --> 00:05:16.080
A nice breakfast will cheer you up.

17
00:05:18.791 --> 00:05:21.293
I'm not getting upset over...

18
00:05:22.711 --> 00:05:25.422
What is that (?)

19
00:05:25.589 --> 00:05:29.134
- It's bacon.
- I know it's bacon.

20
00:05:29.301 --> 00:05:32.054
What have you done to it?

21
00:05:32.221 --> 00:05:37.601
You said you didn't like the grease
from fried bacon. So I boiled it.

22
00:05:37.768 --> 00:05:41.230
(RADIO - POP MUSIC)

23
00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:48.612
What is Lane doing up
at this hour on a Sunday?

24
00:05:48.779 --> 00:05:52.241
Doesn't he turn to dust
if the sun hits him?

25
00:05:52.408 --> 00:05:56.578
It's try-outs for the ski team.
He's going to Mount Brodie with Beth.

26
00:05:56.745 --> 00:06:00.708
Sure. he can't do anything
without that girl.

27
00:06:00.874 --> 00:06:04.253
I tell you. Jenny.
that boy is obsessed.

28
00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:08.006
Now. honey... Obsessed?

29
00:06:20.769 --> 00:06:24.106
Do we not throw empty things away?

30
00:06:25.149 --> 00:06:27.151
Oh.

31
00:06:44.918 --> 00:06:48.213
What in the name
of all that's holy?

32
00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:52.676
Badger likes the prizes you get
from cutting the coupons out.

33
00:06:52.843 --> 00:06:57.139
- He's mailing them today.
- Can't you wait until?

34
00:07:07.566 --> 00:07:12.237
Lane. the closet door can be closed
as well as opened.

35
00:07:12.863 --> 00:07:14.281
Ooh!

36
00:07:14.448 --> 00:07:18.619
- Sorry. Dad.
- Lane. your breakfast is getting cold.

37
00:07:18.786 --> 00:07:22.748
Thanks. I can't have breakfast.
I got trials today.

38
00:07:22.915 --> 00:07:25.501
I don't want to throw up again.

39
00:07:25.667 --> 00:07:29.463
I had to buy that guy a new hat
last time. Bye. Dad.

40
00:07:31.131 --> 00:07:33.008
Lane!

41
00:07:33.175 --> 00:07:38.597
I would like to meet you tonight
to discuss the future of that vehicle.

42
00:07:38.764 --> 00:07:44.603
which you purchased months ago.
yet has darkened our drive ever since.

43
00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:48.232
Noted. Talk to you tonight.
Gotta pick up Beth.

44
00:08:08.794 --> 00:08:10.462
(SIGHS)

45
00:08:18.053 --> 00:08:20.139
Ricky! Ricky!

46
00:08:24.309 --> 00:08:28.689
Ricky! Don't be so shy! Come here.

47
00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:37.531
Monique. this is Ricky.

48
00:08:37.698 --> 00:08:43.954
Ricky. this is Monique. the French
student who'll be staying with us.

49
00:08:45.789 --> 00:08:48.292
(GARGLED SNORT)

50
00:09:04.725 --> 00:09:06.435
Ah!

51
00:09:07.061 --> 00:09:09.438
It's an awesome spectacle.

52
00:09:09.605 --> 00:09:13.067
an audacious display
of seething opponents.

53
00:09:13.233 --> 00:09:15.319
once again. parallel.

54
00:09:15.486 --> 00:09:20.491
in an obstinate attempt
to prove superiority of the roads.

55
00:09:20.657 --> 00:09:23.535
unequalled in our lifetime.

56
00:09:23.702 --> 00:09:29.041
The crowds swell with anticipation
as the lights turn green!

57
00:09:39.051 --> 00:09:43.180
You stupid bonehead! You idiot!

58
00:09:43.347 --> 00:09:46.100
- Sir...
- Get out of this car!

59
00:09:46.266 --> 00:09:49.019
If he asks me. I'll go out with him.

60
00:09:49.186 --> 00:09:51.271
I mean. he skis the K-12.

61
00:09:51.897 --> 00:09:54.817
Yeah. he's so boss!

62
00:09:54.983 --> 00:10:00.698
Lane? I'll tell him after trials. You
know how he gets when he gets upset.

63
00:10:00.864 --> 00:10:06.078
Yeah... from the chairlifts! He had
to buy the guy a new hat last time.

64
00:10:06.245 --> 00:10:07.579
(CAR HORN)

65
00:10:07.746 --> 00:10:12.209
Lane's here. I gotta go.
I'll call you later. Bye.

66
00:10:44.908 --> 00:10:50.956
He's the only person that's skied
the K-12 from the glacier and lived.

67
00:11:13.604 --> 00:11:16.523
Man! What a hunk!

68
00:11:28.035 --> 00:11:33.874
Your time has to be under 58 seconds
to even be considered for the team.

69
00:11:34.041 --> 00:11:39.046
Your time will be gauged along with
a rating of one to ten on your style.

70
00:11:39.213 --> 00:11:43.884
judged solely by me and my vast
expertise of skiing technique.

71
00:11:44.051 --> 00:11:48.597
Why don't you sorry-looking hopefuls
make your way up the hill?

72
00:11:48.764 --> 00:11:54.478
The girls can keep me company
till it's time for you to take the track.

73
00:11:54.645 --> 00:11:57.648
Who'd like to... hold my clipboard?

74
00:11:59.983 --> 00:12:02.194
What's your name?

75
00:12:02.361 --> 00:12:08.867
- Charles De Mar.
- Shut up. geek. What's your name?

76
00:12:09.034 --> 00:12:12.538
- Beth.
- That's my favourite name.

77
00:12:15.457 --> 00:12:18.794
- Roy Stalin. How you doing?
- Lane Myer.

78
00:12:18.961 --> 00:12:21.714
You and I share one common desire.

79
00:12:23.048 --> 00:12:28.804
to be part of the well-oiled machinery
that is Greendale School Ski Team.

80
00:12:28.971 --> 00:12:31.056
The desire for victory!

81
00:12:31.223 --> 00:12:33.767
- Well...
- Let's see what you got!

82
00:12:43.444 --> 00:12:46.280
- Ready up there?
- We're all set.

83
00:12:46.447 --> 00:12:50.826
- What is the next victim's name?
- Myer. Lane Myer.

84
00:12:50.993 --> 00:12:55.497
- Is that as in Oscar Mayer?
- That's a roger.

85
00:12:55.664 --> 00:13:01.795
Beth. you were standing with Oscar.
Is he your main wiener man?

86
00:13:01.962 --> 00:13:07.760
Don't listen to Stalin. kid.
He's a punk. Now you show him.

87
00:13:07.926 --> 00:13:10.679
Show him how a skier really skis.

88
00:13:10.846 --> 00:13:14.099
- We're sending him down.
- Counting down.

89
00:13:15.225 --> 00:13:17.853
Drei. frei. go!

90
00:13:44.213 --> 00:13:48.384
Too bad. Real close. Next.

91
00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:54.348
<i>(BETH) Lane. I think we should talk.</i>
<i>We've been seeing a lot of each other.</i>

92
00:13:54.515 --> 00:13:58.686
<i>It's in my interests to go out</i>
<i>with someone more popular.</i>

93
00:13:58.852 --> 00:14:01.689
<i>better-looking. drives a nicer car.</i>

94
00:14:05.275 --> 00:14:09.863
Six months! Six months.
and she just dumps me for him.

95
00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:14.201
For Stalin. just like that!
Six months!

96
00:14:20.082 --> 00:14:24.753
Truly a sight to behold.
A man. beaten.

97
00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:30.634
The once great champ.
now a study in moppishness.

98
00:14:30.801 --> 00:14:36.932
No longer the victory-hungry stallion
we've raced so many times before.

99
00:14:37.099 --> 00:14:41.937
but a pathetic. washed-up.
aged ex-champion.

100
00:14:42.104 --> 00:14:44.189
All right. let's go!

101
00:14:50.112 --> 00:14:52.156
Someone gonna see God.

102
00:14:54.992 --> 00:15:01.623
I want to break your goddamn neck!
Get out! Get out of the car!

103
00:15:06.128 --> 00:15:10.299
- Hello. Lane. How was your day?
- Beth broke up with me.

104
00:15:10.466 --> 00:15:14.011
- That's nice.
- We're through. That's it.

105
00:15:28.776 --> 00:15:31.904
What the hell? Wait a minute here.

106
00:15:32.821 --> 00:15:34.990
Wait. this is death here.

107
00:15:36.867 --> 00:15:41.663
I haven't even been to New York City.
I haven't been anywhere!

108
00:15:52.591 --> 00:15:56.220
Suicide is never the answer.
little trooper.

109
00:15:56.387 --> 00:15:59.515
Greendale is a small town. Lane.

110
00:15:59.682 --> 00:16:03.852
It's a fly speck on the map
on the way to a ski slope.

111
00:16:04.019 --> 00:16:06.647
I can't even get real drugs here!

112
00:16:07.898 --> 00:16:11.985
Stalin's a hero.
the only one who can ski the K-12.

113
00:16:12.152 --> 00:16:15.239
You're a great skier.
but he's incredible.

114
00:16:16.407 --> 00:16:20.577
If I skied the K-12.
do you think she'd take me back?

115
00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:25.416
Now I'm back to suicide again.

116
00:16:30.337 --> 00:16:33.340
<i>(MOM) We're all going</i>
<i>to enjoy this treat.</i>

117
00:16:33.507 --> 00:16:37.136
I got the recipe from
the "Ladies' Home Journal".

118
00:16:37.302 --> 00:16:41.265
The mail got wet.
so some of the pages ran together.

119
00:16:41.432 --> 00:16:44.643
I improvised
with my own little ideas.

120
00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:48.272
You see. it's got... raisins in it.

121
00:16:48.439 --> 00:16:50.524
You like raisins!

122
00:16:52.568 --> 00:16:57.781
There is still one more thing
I'd like to discuss with Lane.

123
00:16:57.948 --> 00:17:00.534
The subject here...

124
00:17:02.745 --> 00:17:05.873
...is the mystery car...

125
00:17:06.915 --> 00:17:09.293
Thank you.

126
00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:15.549
...which. even as we speak. darkens
our domain under a mouldy tarp.

127
00:17:15.716 --> 00:17:19.345
- You know the car of which I speak?
- Yeah...

128
00:17:19.511 --> 00:17:23.140
Let me refresh your memory.
Cast your mind back.

129
00:17:23.307 --> 00:17:25.976
It's a crisp September morning.

130
00:17:26.143 --> 00:17:29.355
You borrowed $200
to purchase the car.

131
00:17:29.521 --> 00:17:32.816
because your girlfriend Beth
said it was...

132
00:17:32.983 --> 00:17:35.319
I believe the term was "tasty".

133
00:17:35.486 --> 00:17:40.407
Since then. that "tasty" car
has slept in an auto-cocoon

134
00:17:40.574 --> 00:17:42.659
on my front lawn!

135
00:17:44.078 --> 00:17:46.830
I'll get around to it.

136
00:17:46.997 --> 00:17:51.627
Lane. have you seen the student
who's staying at the Smiths' house?

137
00:17:51.794 --> 00:17:55.798
Go over and welcome her to our town.
She'd like that.

138
00:17:55.964 --> 00:18:01.178
Mrs Smith probably got her so that
her weird son could see a real girl!

139
00:18:01.345 --> 00:18:07.059
He never goes outdoors. just sits
in that house and crochets all day.

140
00:18:07.226 --> 00:18:10.854
The Chapmans had their student
for six months.

141
00:18:11.021 --> 00:18:15.442
- He became a son to Jules and Irene.
- That kid from El Salvador?

142
00:18:15.609 --> 00:18:19.238
Can I be excused?
I'm not feeling well.

143
00:18:19.405 --> 00:18:21.657
I'm just gonna be excused.

144
00:18:33.544 --> 00:18:36.088
I can't figure it out. Badger.

145
00:18:36.255 --> 00:18:40.926
You seem smart. Why do you waste
your time with this kid stuff?

146
00:18:43.887 --> 00:18:45.973
You're almost eight.

147
00:18:52.730 --> 00:18:54.273
OK.

148
00:19:03.782 --> 00:19:07.536
Beth... It was love at first sight.

149
00:19:13.083 --> 00:19:19.298
Red Dog. Red Dog! 92! 74! 16! 43!
Bring it home. Momma!

150
00:19:49.578 --> 00:19:51.663
- Hi.
- Hi.

151
00:19:56.668 --> 00:20:00.631
- So. how do you like Greendale?
- Fine.

152
00:20:03.592 --> 00:20:09.098
- You find the school system adequate?
- School hasn't started yet.

153
00:20:10.683 --> 00:20:15.896
<i>She itched her nose. A message to me</i>
<i>that there was something on my nose?</i>

154
00:20:16.063 --> 00:20:19.775
<i>That's funny.</i>
<i>He wiped his nose after I did.</i>

155
00:20:19.942 --> 00:20:25.572
<i>Maybe I got some dirt on my nose.</i>
<i>He's too embarrassed to tell me!</i>

156
00:20:25.739 --> 00:20:27.825
<i>I must look sickening!</i>

157
00:20:28.826 --> 00:20:33.205
<i>There she goes again!</i>
<i>What could it be? Relish on my nose?</i>

158
00:20:33.372 --> 00:20:38.043
<i>How gross! She might think</i>
<i>it's a... Oh. not that. please!</i>

159
00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:41.839
<i>Please don't let it be a booger.</i>
<i>Please. God!</i>

160
00:21:05.696 --> 00:21:11.243
I don't get it.
How could she throw away six months?

161
00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:15.372
I mean. six months. just like that!

162
00:21:17.166 --> 00:21:22.921
No explanation. no reason.
Just... Just throw it away!

163
00:21:23.088 --> 00:21:26.008
How can you throw away six months?

164
00:21:26.175 --> 00:21:29.386
When you're... in love with someone...

165
00:21:30.721 --> 00:21:35.684
Six months! I'm history!
Just like that. I'm gone.

166
00:21:37.144 --> 00:21:42.358
She's probably just testing me.
Big test. That's probably it.

167
00:21:42.524 --> 00:21:46.862
- (DOORBELL)
- That's her. That's her!

168
00:21:52.076 --> 00:21:55.204
- Johnny...
- Four weeks.

169
00:21:55.371 --> 00:21:59.541
Twenty papers.
That's two dollars. plus tip.

170
00:21:59.708 --> 00:22:01.919
I don't have a dime. Sorry.

171
00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:06.382
I didn't ask for a dime! Two dollars!

172
00:22:07.966 --> 00:22:10.052
Well. it's funny.

173
00:22:10.219 --> 00:22:14.390
My mom had to leave early
to take my brother to school.

174
00:22:14.556 --> 00:22:17.393
Two dollars... cash!

175
00:22:17.559 --> 00:22:22.773
The problem is that my little brother
got an arm caught in the microwave.

176
00:22:22.940 --> 00:22:26.568
My grandmother dropped acid
and freaked out

177
00:22:26.735 --> 00:22:29.655
and hijacked a bus full of penguins.

178
00:22:29.822 --> 00:22:34.410
It's kind of a family crisis.
so come back later. Great.

179
00:22:34.576 --> 00:22:39.415
<i>(CAR RADIO: "BREAKING UP</i>
<i>IS HARD TO DO")</i>

180
00:22:41.417 --> 00:22:44.503
<i># Breaking up is hard to do... #

181
00:22:44.670 --> 00:22:47.798
<i># Don't take your love... #

182
00:22:49.258 --> 00:22:51.343
<i># And she's gone... #

183
00:22:51.510 --> 00:22:54.430
<i># Fifty ways to leave your lover... #

184
00:22:54.596 --> 00:22:57.016
<i># It hurts so bad... #

185
00:22:57.182 --> 00:23:01.478
<i># They say that breaking up</i>
<i>is hard to do... #

186
00:23:05.399 --> 00:23:10.612
<i>The three cardinal.</i>
<i>trapezoidal formations.</i>

187
00:23:10.779 --> 00:23:13.907
<i>hereto made orientable</i>
<i>in our diagram</i>

188
00:23:14.074 --> 00:23:20.080
<i>by connecting the various points.</i>
<i>HIGK. PEGQ and LMNO.</i>

189
00:23:20.247 --> 00:23:24.418
creating our geometric
configurations.

190
00:23:24.585 --> 00:23:28.881
which have no properties.
but with location...

191
00:23:29.048 --> 00:23:30.466
(ALL) Aah!

192
00:23:30.632 --> 00:23:38.432
...are equal to the described
triangle CAB quintuplicated.

193
00:23:38.599 --> 00:23:40.684
Therefore...

194
00:23:42.061 --> 00:23:46.940
...the five triangles composing
the aforementioned NIGH

195
00:23:47.107 --> 00:23:51.820
each are equal to the triangle CAB
in this geometric concept!

196
00:23:51.987 --> 00:23:55.449
Therefore. in a like manner.

197
00:23:55.616 --> 00:24:01.872
the geometric metaphors can
derive a repeated vectoral sum.

198
00:24:02.039 --> 00:24:04.416
This was your assignment.

199
00:24:04.583 --> 00:24:09.213
I would like to see the results. please.

200
00:24:09.380 --> 00:24:11.215
Take them out!

201
00:24:35.322 --> 00:24:36.865
Oops.

202
00:24:37.032 --> 00:24:40.160
- Sophia...
- Oh! Oh! Oh!

203
00:24:40.327 --> 00:24:43.372
- Oh. please!
- And... Buster.

204
00:24:43.539 --> 00:24:47.042
- Me! Me! Please!
- And... Beth.

205
00:24:49.336 --> 00:24:52.965
- And...
- Oh. please. please. please!

206
00:24:53.132 --> 00:24:58.137
Mr Myer. Please join us
at the blackboard

207
00:24:58.303 --> 00:25:02.516
and show us your solution
to this paltry geometric dilemma.

208
00:25:21.118 --> 00:25:24.496
- (SCREECH)
- (ALL) Oh...!

209
00:25:25.664 --> 00:25:27.750
Oh. sorry.

210
00:25:59.531 --> 00:26:03.160
Lane. would you relax?!
It's just our virginity!

211
00:26:03.327 --> 00:26:05.412
Oh. I agree. totally.

212
00:26:05.579 --> 00:26:10.250
We should tell someone or do
something or get my Dad's Polaroid.

213
00:26:11.001 --> 00:26:13.087
- What was that?
- What?

214
00:26:13.253 --> 00:26:15.339
I heard something.

215
00:26:15.506 --> 00:26:20.719
You're in the most secluded place in
the northern hemisphere. We're alone.

216
00:26:23.138 --> 00:26:24.515
Come on.

217
00:26:27.893 --> 00:26:32.898
- What's wrong?
- That thing I put on me. it broke.

218
00:26:34.149 --> 00:26:36.235
Broke? It broke?!

219
00:26:36.402 --> 00:26:41.198
- Take it easy. I'll buy a new one.
- I don't want a new one!

220
00:26:41.365 --> 00:26:43.659
I'm sorry!

221
00:26:48.789 --> 00:26:50.999
(BELL)

222
00:26:51.166 --> 00:26:52.751
(ALL) Aw!

223
00:26:52.918 --> 00:26:56.672
Now. now. now.
I'll see you all tomorrow.

224
00:26:56.839 --> 00:27:01.844
Remember to memorise pages
39 to 110 for tomorrow's lesson.

225
00:27:02.011 --> 00:27:04.596
- (ALL) All right!
- Cool!

226
00:27:04.763 --> 00:27:08.100
(GIRL) Mr Kerber
really just makes geometry live.

227
00:27:15.649 --> 00:27:21.363
Lane. listen. I've been thinking
about what you told me last night.

228
00:27:21.530 --> 00:27:25.242
- I've decided I'm going to help you.
- How?

229
00:27:25.409 --> 00:27:31.457
I've been going to this high school
for seven and a half years.

230
00:27:31.623 --> 00:27:33.542
I'm no dummy.

231
00:27:33.709 --> 00:27:36.837
I know high-school girls.

232
00:27:37.004 --> 00:27:42.009
Two things. One. how about your sax?

233
00:27:42.176 --> 00:27:45.721
- I mean. Roy plays the guitar.
