- Lane. where have you been?

527
00:59:30.834 --> 00:59:36.048
We've all been waiting for you.
Come and sit right down here.

528
00:59:38.926 --> 00:59:42.930
- Have you met Monique?
- Hi.

529
00:59:43.097 --> 00:59:48.310
In honour of our special guest.
I've created Dinner "Mon Doux".

530
00:59:48.477 --> 00:59:53.315
First. we have... Franch fries!

531
00:59:54.566 --> 00:59:58.946
And... Franch dressing!

532
01:00:00.531 --> 01:00:03.784
And... Franch bread!

533
01:00:03.951 --> 01:00:08.288
And to drink... Peru!

534
01:00:10.916 --> 01:00:15.796
You really do go to the outer limits
to make an impression!

535
01:00:18.882 --> 01:00:22.553
Monique. enjoying your stay
in our town?

536
01:00:25.139 --> 01:00:29.309
Are you enjoying your stay
in our town?

537
01:00:29.476 --> 01:00:32.938
- She doesn't speak English.
- Course she does.

538
01:00:33.105 --> 01:00:37.693
- Are you enjoying your stay?
- She don't speak a word.

539
01:00:37.860 --> 01:00:41.905
I thought these students
had to speak some English!

540
01:00:42.072 --> 01:00:44.992
As we're discovering in our house.

541
01:00:45.159 --> 01:00:51.248
you don't need words to speak
the "international" language.

542
01:00:51.415 --> 01:00:54.043
- Right. Ricky?
- Uh?

543
01:00:54.335 --> 01:00:57.463
The "international" language!

544
01:00:57.629 --> 01:00:59.715
You know!

545
01:01:02.509 --> 01:01:06.013
Love. the language of love!

546
01:01:06.180 --> 01:01:11.852
Monique and Ricky have a regular
cross-continental romance brewing.

547
01:01:12.936 --> 01:01:17.316
Him? And her? That makes sense.

548
01:01:20.611 --> 01:01:24.031
Pardonne-moi.
Où sont les toilettes?

549
01:01:24.198 --> 01:01:26.950
- What's that mean?
- S'il-vous-plaît?

550
01:01:27.117 --> 01:01:30.871
I think she wants
to use the bathroom.

551
01:01:31.038 --> 01:01:36.710
It's down the hall.
second door... on the left. Monique.

552
01:01:41.090 --> 01:01:45.594
Jennifer. this is fabulous liqueur.

553
01:01:45.761 --> 01:01:50.432
Reminds me of the moonshine
Ricky's dead papa used to make.

554
01:01:50.599 --> 01:01:54.061
- God bless him!
- Mrs Smith. no. wait!

555
01:01:57.106 --> 01:02:01.944
I'm sorry your mom blew up. Ricky.
Doctor said she'd be OK.

556
01:02:02.111 --> 01:02:07.074
I guess she just won't be able
to eat any spicy foods for a while.

557
01:02:13.247 --> 01:02:15.332
Oh. no. Not now.

558
01:02:18.627 --> 01:02:21.630
- What do they want?
- A race.

559
01:02:22.798 --> 01:02:28.178
- Lane Myer. the kid from Greendale.
- Here's a good example.

560
01:02:28.345 --> 01:02:30.931
Two brothers. One speaks no English.

561
01:02:31.098 --> 01:02:34.727
The other learned English
from watching sports.

562
01:02:34.893 --> 01:02:39.356
Which is better? Speaking no English
or speaking Howard Cosell?

563
01:02:39.523 --> 01:02:44.361
The chances seem slim
that this once great has the nerve.

564
01:02:44.528 --> 01:02:46.780
the desire to win.

565
01:02:46.947 --> 01:02:50.909
You must obey the speed limits.
A car is not a toy.

566
01:02:57.958 --> 01:03:02.046
- We're tanking. guys!
- <i>Myer takes the lead.</i>

567
01:03:02.212 --> 01:03:07.343
- <i>This could go on Myer's right.</i>
- Lane Myer. slow down!

568
01:03:10.763 --> 01:03:14.558
<i>Lane Myer takes the lead!</i>

569
01:03:14.725 --> 01:03:17.728
<i>It's close. very. very close!</i>

570
01:03:47.257 --> 01:03:51.637
Oh. my God! Ricky's dead!
Ricky. are you dead?

571
01:03:51.804 --> 01:03:55.432
I think he's dead.
Monique. I'm sorry.

572
01:03:55.599 --> 01:03:57.685
I'm sorry I didn't...

573
01:04:00.312 --> 01:04:03.190
